$","h1",null,{"className":"font-display text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem)] leading-[0.95] tracking-[0.02em] text-white mb-5","children":"SATS: The Most Powerful Manifestation Technique You're Not Using"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body italic text-grey-DEFAULT text-lg leading-relaxed","children":"Every night, there's a 5-10 minute window between waking and sleep where your brain enters Theta waves and your subconscious becomes fully receptive. This is SATS — and it's your direct line to reality creation."}]]}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-14 px-6 md:px-14","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto","children":[["$","h2","0",{"className":"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"What Is SATS?"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["SATS stands for State Akin to Sleep — Neville Goddard's term for the hypnagogic state you pass through every night as you drift toward sleep. During this window, your brainwaves shift from Beta (waking, analytical) through Alpha (relaxed) into Theta (deeply relaxed, pre-sleep)."]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The Theta state is significant for one reason: your critical factor — the analytical, skeptical part of your mind — goes offline. The gatekeeper falls asleep before you do."]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["This means whatever you impress upon your subconscious in this window goes in ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"without resistance."}],""]}],["$","h2","4",{"className":"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The Neuroscience"}],["$","p","5",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["When your brain is in Theta waves (4-8 Hz), you are in the same state as:"]}],["$","ul","6",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-3 my-6","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Deep meditation practitioners"}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Children under the age of 7 (which is why early programming is so sticky)"}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Hypnotherapy subjects"}]]}]]}],["$","p","7",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["This is not mysticism. EEG studies consistently show that Theta states correlate with heightened subconscious receptivity and accelerated learning. Advertisers, therapists, and military trainers have known this for decades."]}],["$","p","8",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Neville Goddard discovered it through direct experience decades before the research caught up."]}],["$","h2","9",{"className":"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"How to Enter SATS"}],["$","p","10",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"1. Time it right."}],"\nThe best SATS window is in the 5-10 minutes as you lie down for sleep. Don't try to force it during the day. The natural relaxation response of your body at night is your ally."]}],["$","p","11",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"2. Relax the body."}],"\nLie flat, close your eyes, and consciously release tension from your feet to your scalp. Don't rush this. You're not trying to meditate — you're letting the body do what it does naturally."]}],["$","p","12",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"3. Choose your scene."}],"\nPick a single scene that implies your wish is fulfilled. Not a movie — one moment. Hearing someone congratulate you. Looking at your phone and seeing a text that confirms everything is fine. Feeling the key to your new home in your hand."]}],["$","p","13",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"4. Make it first-person and present."}],"\nYou're not watching yourself in the scene. You're *in* it. The imagery is from your own eyes, as if it's happening right now."]}],["$","p","14",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"5. Loop the scene."}],"\nRepeat the scene gently, like a lullaby. Don't analyze it. Don't question it. Just let it play. Fall asleep in the scene, or as close to it as possible."]}],["$","h2","15",{"className":"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"Common Mistakes"}],["$","ul","16",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-3 my-6","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"**Making the scene too long or complex.** Simplicity is power. One clear moment of implication."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"**Watching yourself from outside.** You must be inside the experience, not observing it."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"**Trying too hard.** Effort creates tension. Tension blocks the Theta state. Let go."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"**Quitting too soon.** Current reality is an echo of past thoughts, often 60-90 days behind. Persistence is required."}]]}]]}],["$","h2","17",{"className":"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The Compound Effect"}],["$","p","18",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["SATS done consistently creates what might be called a subconscious consensus. Every night you add another impression to the new state. Over weeks, the old programs are overwritten. The RAS recalibrates. And reality begins to shift — first in small ways, then in unmistakable ones."]}],["$","p","19",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["One session is a seed. Thirty sessions is a garden."]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"px-6 md:px-14 pb-14","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-black-2 border-2 border-orange-DEFAULT p-8 md:p-12 text-center","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":20,"height":20,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill"